{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 611 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "e06bd84923467c614f21fb62b15622f93e44349ffc84cdbaa6797c28eba89195" :edb/db-before-t 610 :edb/db-after-t 611 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533923 50 #inst "2026-10-05T13:16:22.825Z" 13194139533923 true] [17592186068613 1020 #edb/ref 17592186266145 13194139533923 true] [17592186068613 1020 #edb/ref 17592186266148 13194139533923 true] [17592186068615 1020 #edb/ref 17592186266152 13194139533923 true] [17592186069170 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533923 true] [17592186069170 1145 "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ so applying  L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{e}^{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{[2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]}^{′}}{[{e}^{x}]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{2}{x})}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2}{x{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533923 true] [17592186069434 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533923 true] [17592186069434 1145 "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{-\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x} & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)]}^{′}}{[\\operatorname{csc}⁡x]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\cancel{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266145 1017 #edb/ref 17592186266146 13194139533923 true] [17592186266145 1089 "q-314152" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266145 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533923 true] [17592186266145 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\,{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x{e}^{2x}-x+3{x}^{2}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266145 1113 #uuid "e190c4a3-1ee2-5dcd-b3fa-376f55f2ec5b" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266145 1145 "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x{e}^{2x}-x+3{x}^{2}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[x{e}^{2x}-x+3{x}^{2}]^{′}}{[{sin}^{2}⁡x]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(1+2x){e}^{2x}-1+6x}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(1+2x){e}^{2x}-1+6x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x{e}^{2x}-x+3{x}^{2}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(1+2x){e}^{2x}-1+6x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[(1+2x){e}^{2x}-1+6x]^{′}}{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(4+4x){e}^{2x}+6}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(4+0){e}^{0}+6}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+6}{2} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266146 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266147 13194139533923 true] [17592186266146 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533923 true] [17592186266146 1041 "field-1" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266146 1104 #edb/ref 17592186266147 13194139533923 true] [17592186266146 1110 #uuid "988ea093-d38d-51ab-8d06-7e5be72e5b6a" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266147 1034 "5" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266147 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533923 true] [17592186266147 1111 #uuid "e181f272-c259-5dfe-9f39-b3b9e5618d5f" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266148 1017 #edb/ref 17592186266149 13194139533923 true] [17592186266148 1089 "q-336897" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266148 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533923 true] [17592186266148 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\,{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{({x}^{2}-5)^{2}-48x+128}{{x}^{2}-6x+9}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266148 1113 #uuid "4e31f629-06c9-5847-8488-ea8d7bd593df" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266148 1145 "If we plug in $x=3$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{({x}^{2}-5)^{2}-48x+128}{{x}^{2}-6x+9} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{[({x}^{2}-5)^{2}-48x+128]}^{′}}{[{x}^{2}-6x+9]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{4x({x}^{2}-5)-48}{2x-6} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{2{x}^{3}-10x-24}{x-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{({x}^{2}-5)^{2}-48x+128}{{x}^{2}-6x+9} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{2{x}^{3}-10x-24}{x-3} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{[2{x}^{3}-10x-24]}^{′}}{{[x-3]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{6{x}^{2}-10}{1} \\\\  & =6(3)^{2}-10 \\\\  & =44.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266150 13194139533923 true] [17592186266149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186266151 13194139533923 true] [17592186266149 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533923 true] [17592186266149 1041 "field-1" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266149 1104 #edb/ref 17592186266151 13194139533923 true] [17592186266149 1110 #uuid "74e7b4d9-3a93-54ee-942e-14e16a7bc102" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266150 1034 "43" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266150 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533923 true] [17592186266150 1111 #uuid "440eb8e0-c5a3-524a-9bf3-4130be95649a" 13194139533923 true] [17592186266151 1034 "44" 13194